  "input_routing_findings": [
    "Staging preserves original full-frame image bytes. The native trainer receives those paths and delegates rectangular batching and standard augmentation to the pinned trainer.",
    "Recorded samples have 736 by 1280 spatial tensor shape after preprocessing; these sample records do not claim that every batch was instrumented.",
    "The native R37 runner supplies no experiment input transform or row-crop transform. Geometric augmentation can move, clip or resample frame content; this audit does not claim every background pixel survives every augmentation.",
    "Ordinary evaluation passes each full original image path to model.predict with imgsz1280, rectTrue, batch1, FP32 and ordinary NMS. Saved outputs return original 1280 by 720 coordinates.",
    "Boxes are supervision targets, not masks that remove all pixels outside their boundaries from the model input. The cropped PDF panels are human review views."
  ],
  "target_definition": {
    "policy": "baomai-visible-front-v1",
    "rule": "Tight axis-aligned envelope of supported visible front-face material, clipped to the image; rack, gripper, neighboring cassette and guessed hidden extent do not set its outer edges.",
    "internal_background": "An enclosing rectangle may necessarily contain background or an occluder between visible parts or beside a slanted front.",
    "recommendation": "Keep target boundaries physically consistent; retain surrounding scene context in the input. Evaluate new capture sessions/backgrounds separately before claiming generalization."
  },
